3+2eps reads as 3+2eps
(dual 1/2 -1) prints as 1/2-eps
(string->number "2-eps") = 2-eps
(+ d 1) = 4+eps
(+ 1 d) = 4+eps
(* d d) = 9+6eps
(* 1/2 d) = 3/2+1/2eps
(- d 0.5) = 2.5+eps
(/ 1 d) = 1/3-1/9eps
(= d 3+eps) = #t
(< 2 d 4) = #t
(number? d) = #t
(exact? d) = #t
(real? d) = #f
(exact? 1.5+eps) = #f
the derivative of x^3 at 2 is 12
the derivative of (x^2+1)/(x-3) at 1 is -3/2
... and at 1/2 it is -3/5
